      "side": 1,
      "message": "This will break bitbang because you need CCD_ENABLE_UART_EC | CCD_ENABLE_UART_EC_BITBANG for the RX part.\n\nI think having the CCD_ENABLE_UART_EC* flags control both enabling the uart and enabling the usb when they need to be enabled at separate times is complicating this a lot.\nI think it would be clearer if we had two new flags to track the usb part of this.\nCCD_ENABLE_USB_EC and CCD_ENABLE_USB_EC_TX.\nThis would mean you don\u0027t need to change the CCD_ENABLE_UART_EC logic as much. You would need to add logic for determining if usb is enabled and a function to make usb_usart enabled/disabled and readonly.\nI think this would be more consistent with how ccd_state_change currently works.",
